# formal/: the Lean formalization

Machine-checked proofs for {{project.name}}. The rules for working here are in
[../docs/discipline/lean.md](../docs/discipline/lean.md).

{{#if stack.lake_path}}
## The Lean project

The Lake project is `{{stack.lake_path}}` (set as `lake_path` under `[stack]` in
`project.toml`). Build it with `bin/lean-build`, never a bare `lake build`; check a finished
result with `bin/lean-build --axioms <Module> <declaration>`. Search the library by
declaration name with `bin/lib-find <name-regex>`.
If `lake_path` points to an existing project outside this repository, init-math did not touch
it. Commit its `lean-toolchain` and `lake-manifest.json` in that project, or add it here as a
submodule.
{{else}}
## Setting up the Lean project (not done yet)

No Lean project exists yet. When you are ready, run these yourself (they download the
library cache, several GB).

In the `formal/` directory (create it if missing):

```sh
lake new Proofs math        # creates Proofs/ using Mathlib; one word, no hyphens
```

`lake new` also writes the `lean-toolchain` pin. Then, in `formal/Proofs`:

```sh
lake exe cache get          # fetch compiled library files instead of building them
```

Then set `lake_path = "formal/Proofs"` under `[stack]` in `project.toml`. After that,
`bin/lean-build` builds the project and `bin/lib-find` searches its library.
{{/if}}

## Layout

- One file per topic under the project's source directory; each top-level result carries a
  docstring naming the statement it formalizes (a paper's theorem number, or a link to the
  note that states it).
- A result counts as done only when it has no `sorry` and `#print axioms` lists nothing
  beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.
- Keep the library version pinned (`lean-toolchain` and the lake manifest are committed in
  the Lean project's repository; for an outside project, commit them there or add it as a
  submodule); bump it deliberately, in its own commit.
- Each top-level result's docstring names the statement{{#if modules.conjectures}} or conjecture id{{/if}} it formalizes{{#if modules.conjectures}}
  (for example C003){{/if}}.
